# Rockman CX (JP) dialogue table, bank $26 scripts.  JP text bytes are tile numbers $20-$FF in the dialogue
# pattern table; each script loads its own 16-glyph pages with op 04 [CHR hi,bank,dst] (dst $12 = codes $20-$2F, etc.).
# Codes therefore change meaning per script.  This table lists the most common page for each code row;
# rows marked "varies" are per-script kanji pages (decode with build/research/cx/cx-text2/turns.py, which follows
# the CHR ops and maps glyph bitmaps to characters via jp_glyphs.tsv).  Control codes are as in the EN table,
# except 07 [NUM] takes 5 argument bytes and 0D is unused.
# codes 20-2F: page bank $29 $A000 (ROM 0x52000), loaded by 13 of 24 CHR ops for this row (varies)
20=が
21=な
22=い
23=の
24=つ
25=そ
26=を
27=た
28=…
29=！
2A=、
2B=。
2C=ど
2D=は
2E=？
2F=に
# codes 30-3F: page bank $29 $A200 (ROM 0x52200), loaded by 12 of 27 CHR ops for this row (varies)
